      "writtenOn": "2021-12-23T22:18:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We\u0027ll definitely need something like scratch keys. Essentially the scratch key just represents the key that describes the resource. That is something we\u0027ll need whether or not it specifically ends up getting called a scratch key or not.\n\nYeah I think we will want to update lots of this and rethink how we want to do stuff. The plan for now is to not be caching proxies ever. Paths in graphite do not to use these keys and we can set up something simpler. For the mask filters its easy enough to change what goes into the key, I feel like ResourceKey is a pretty good abstraction around a key of known fixed size.",
